From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:21:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 72/72] server: a call to an undeclared name must be whole;
 stray text in its XML or GLM markup keeps it as text

2d00471eb let an undeclared function name through for every whole envelope, but the parallel parse
(payload with complete = false) drops stray text inside XML and GLM calls before callName sees them. With only
`shell` declared, `<tool_call><function=bash>junk</function></tool_call>` came back as bash({}) with its text
removed, in whole and streamed replies, where 8e744bf70 kept it as text; single-call mode already refused it.

Call carries `whole` (nothing but the call's markup): functionBlock and glmCall set it from their residue, and
callName accepts an undeclared name only from a whole call. A declared call keeps the parallel parse's leniency;
DSML, JSON and Gemma calls were already strict.

Tests: six malformed undeclared shapes (stray text before, between and after XML parameters, an unclosed
parameter, GLM text after a value, a GLM key with no value) stay text in both call modes, and whitespace near
misses still go out as calls; an HTTP test sends both sets whole and streamed, one-call and parallel. The GLM
pairs test compares the declared name only, since an undeclared name with stray text is now text by design.

The G line's port of public 12257eb51.
